A||||3||BBBAD GT||Low Temp Fan Switch Help||||1||
Z||000000||BBBAD GT||07-15-2000||07:26 PM||||Went to put this sucker on today, and I got a little confused where its at.  I have a 87 V6 service manual, and it said the 'switch' is right below the thermostat housing.  OK, found what looks like it, but the electrical connection is a typical GM weather pack thingy with two small connections.  This low temp switch (Rodney Dickman's) has a round connection on it, and they look like it wouldn't fit at all.  Am I looking in the right spot?  Thanks for the help.<P><P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||07-15-2000||09:27 PM||||It'a just about at the base of the thermostst housing -single grn/wht wire. Looking from the water pump side it's just to the left of the 2 wire one.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BBBAD GT||07-16-2000||01:02 PM||||Found it.  Thanks for the input.  Can't tell you enough how valuable this Forum is.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodney||07-16-2000||03:11 PM||||The fan switch is the one closer to the thermostat housing. It will not fit in the second hole from the thermostat. That hole is a slightly smaller thread size. That sensor also has a 2 wire connector on it. <P>Rodney||||reg||1
